ocular-anterior, which is also important, and a vestibulo-vestibular line, which is related to this line here.

178
00:22:46.055 --> 00:22:56.055
That's why we have saccade research also, or rebalancing research in the anteroposterior plane, or laterality. I told you, when I work, I pay attention

179
00:22:56.055 --> 00:23:05.335
to look at the eye, to look at the eye movement, and to look a little at how the eye will position itself in space, and how sometimes the eye is fixed like that.

180
00:23:05.335 --> 00:23:10.495
So sometimes we can see that people are fixed on a pattern, and in fact it's called the areas.

181
00:23:10.495 --> 00:23:17.565
For example, if we take the right eye first, if you look up and to the right, you are in a visualization of creation.

182
00:23:21.119 --> 00:23:27.279
Whereas if you look horizontally, the eye, will be in relation, you see, these small eye movements.

183
00:23:27.279 --> 00:23:30.319
There, you will have what is called created hearing.

184
00:23:30.319 --> 00:23:39.329
Whereas down, to the right, you will have everything that is called the kinesthetic side, sensation of internal feeling or sensation of external feeling.

185
00:23:42.952 --> 00:23:45.192
Up to the left, it's a memory.

186
00:23:45.892 --> 00:23:50.442
And down and to the left, it's that you are constantly in internal dialogue.

187
00:23:51.766 --> 00:23:57.926
I do a whole liberation work a little at this level, then I do a research work at the level of the eyeball.

188
00:23:57.926 --> 00:24:00.486
And I look at his preferential eye movement.

189
00:24:00.726 --> 00:24:07.766
And there, it will orient me towards visual, auditory, kinesthetic levels, internal, external kinesthetic.

190
00:24:09.686 --> 00:24:13.926
Sometimes, you may have been disturbed in your life by an external noise.

191
00:24:15.266 --> 00:24:24.066
You have your whole postural scheme fixed on it. People who have suffered trauma, for example, during attacks, they are blocked on very deep patterns.

192
00:24:25.220 --> 00:24:27.540
In that, they are sometimes blocked.

193
00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:35.555
And so, sometimes you have to decode them, you have to help them get out of these patterns. To the left, in the middle, auditory memory.

194
00:24:35.555 --> 00:24:38.359
Below, continuous internal dialogue.

